body:
Hi there, 

I´m trying to show the currentRefinedValues in the facet column with the currentRefinedValues widget. Displaying and functionality is fine, but I can´t customize the options for that widget. According to the documentation for my understanding this should work:

```
me.search.addWidget(
            instantsearch.widgets.currentRefinedValues({
                container: '#currentRefinedValues',
                clearAll: 'after',
                options: [{
                    cssClasses: [{
                        root: 'xxx',
                        body: 'bodytest',
                        clearAll: 'clearAllTest',
                        item: 'filter--active'
                    }],
                    templates: [{
                        header: '<h1>test</h1>'
                    }],
                }]
            })
        );
```

However, the "root" options (clearAll, container) work as expected but the parameters in the "options" array are completely ignored.

Has anybody a hint for me what is wrong with my configuration?

Thanks a lot,
Synonymous

comments.body:
Hi @synonymous1984, the syntax should be:

```js
me.search.addWidget(
  instantsearch.widgets.currentRefinedValues({
    container: '#currentRefinedValues',
    clearAll: 'after',
    cssClasses: {
      root: 'xxx',
      body: 'bodytest',
      clearAll: 'clearAllTest',
      item: 'filter--active'
    },
    templates: {
      header: '<h1>test</h1>'
    },
  })
);
```

Did the documentation somehow was misleading? How could we improve it?

Another suggestion for the documentation: template.item does not name the variable which can be used. So how can the item data be shown? itemName, itemCount?

```
me.search.addWidget(
            instantsearch.widgets.currentRefinedValues({
                container: '#currentRefinedValues',
                clearAll: 'after',
                cssClasses: {
                    clearAll: 'clear-all',
                    item: 'filter--active'
                },
                templates: {
                    header: '<div class="shop-sites--headline navigation--headline">Aktive Filter</div>',
                    item: '<span class="filter--active-icon"></span>'
                },
            })
        );
```
